   "source": [
    "# Quantum Parameter Sensitivity Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook evaluates the **sensitivity of the quantum black-box output** $F(X)$ with respect to each learnable parameter $\\theta_i$, using a finite-difference gradient estimator.\n",
    "\n",
    "For a perturbation $\\delta\\theta_i$, we measure:\n",
    "$$S_i^{\\infty} = \\frac{\\|F(X, \\theta + \\delta_i) - F(X, \\theta)\\|_\\infty}{\\delta A}, \\qquad S_i^{2} = \\frac{\\|F(X, \\theta + \\delta_i) - F(X, \\theta)\\|_2}{\\delta A}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "A near-zero sensitivity indicates that the corresponding parameter has **no gradient signal** and cannot be learned.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "**Config :** `quantum_network_config_dudas` | **Estimator :** `GlobalFiniteDifference`"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "setup_header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1 · Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "imports",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-04-15T12:10:56.126702700Z",
     "start_time": "2026-04-15T12:10:37.224599800Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "from dataclasses import fields\n",
    "\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.ticker as mticker\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from zeroth.zeroth_order.gradient_estimators import GlobalFiniteDifferenceConfig\n",
    "\n",
    "from lab.config.quantum_network_config import quantum_network_config_dudas\n",
    "from quantum_simulation.parameters_and_constants import QuantumParameters\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Matplotlib style ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({\n",
    "    \"figure.dpi\": 120,\n",
    "    \"font.family\": \"serif\",\n",
    "    \"axes.spines.top\": False,\n",
    "    \"axes.spines.right\": False,\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "PARAM_NAMES = [f.name for f in fields(QuantumParameters)]\n",
    "print(\"Learnable parameters:\", PARAM_NAMES)"
   ],
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Learnable parameters: ['g_conv', 'g_sq', 'epsilon_a', 'epsilon_b', 'delta_a', 'delta_b']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "execution_count": 1
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "config_header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2 · Configuration"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "config",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-04-15T12:10:56.165085700Z",
     "start_time": "2026-04-15T12:10:56.131710600Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "# ── Experiment hyper-parameters ─────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "DA = 0.01  # finite-difference step size\n",
    "NB_PERIODS = 4  # number of signal periods in the test batch\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Instantiate objects ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "quantum_network = quantum_network_config_dudas.instantiate()\n",
    "gradient_estimator = GlobalFiniteDifferenceConfig(dA=DA).instantiate(\n",
    "    nb_params=quantum_network.nb_params)\n",
    "\n",
    "quantum_network_config_dudas.summary()\n",
    "GlobalFiniteDifferenceConfig(dA=DA).summary()"
   ],
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "QuantumBlackBoxConfig(\n",
      "    name='Q_Network',\n",
      "    jpc_config=JPCConfig(\n",
      "        DIM_A=10,\n",
      "        DIM_B=10,\n",
      "        OMEGA_A=10000.0,\n",
      "        OMEGA_B=9000.0,\n",
      "        KAPPA_A=17,\n",
      "        KAPPA_B=21,\n",
      "        K_AA=0.1,\n",
      "        K_BB=0.1,\n",
      "        K_AB=0.05,\n",
      "        DRIVE_DURATION=0.04,\n",
      "        MEASURE_RESOLUTION=10,\n",
      "        SIMULATION_RESOLUTION=10,\n",
      "        encoding_observable='epsilon'\n",
      "    ),\n",
      "    quantum_parameters=QuantumParametersConfig(\n",
      "        g_conv=700,\n",
      "        g_sq=70,\n",
      "        epsilon_a=65,\n",
      "        epsilon_b=65,\n",
      "        delta_a=10,\n",
      "        delta_b=12\n",
      "    ),\n",
      "    build_f_config=BuildFQuadraturesConfig(\n",
      "\n",
      "    )\n",
      ")\n",
      "GlobalFiniteDifferenceConfig(\n",
      "    dA=0.01\n",
      ")\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "execution_count": 2
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "data_header",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3 · Input Data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "data",
   "metadata": {
    "ExecuteTime": {
     "end_time": "2026-04-15T12:10:56.424188200Z",
     "start_time": "2026-04-15T12:10:56.168086900Z"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "sinus = np.array([-0.7, 0, 0.7, 1, 0.7, 0, -0.7, -1])\n",
    "square = np.array([1, 1, 1, 1, -1, -1, -1, -1])\n",
    "\n",
    "X = np.concatenate((sinus, square, sinus, square, sinus, square, sinus, square, sinus, square))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Input shape  : {X.shape}  →  flattened: {X.shape}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Quick visualisation of the input sequence ────────────────────────────────\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 2.5))\n",
    "ax.step(np.arange(len(X)), X, where=\"mid\", lw=1.2, color=\"steelblue\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Time step\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Amplitude\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(f\"Input signal — {NB_PERIODS} periods ({NB_PERIODS // 2} sinus + {NB_PERIODS // 2} square)\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ],
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Input shape  : (80,)  →  flattened: (80,)\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x300 with 1 Axes>"
